@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+# Kārya 6 source candidate — 2026-10-22
+
+**Status:** This is a development preview. Static source checks are not Flutter compilation, and Android/Windows on-device verification is required. Do not install over valuable local data without a backup.
+
+## Addressed in this candidate
+- Calendar date-selected task creation (with due date), multiple tasks/day, descriptions, scheduled time, and edit entry point.
+- Home quick-add redirects to Tasks.
+- Contextual, replayable tab help; searchable notes board with pinned/color-coded notes, optional automatic saves; fewer phone footer items.
+- Windows navigation: dedicated Journey, Wi-Fi Sync, Help choices.
+- Wi-Fi: pairing network diagnosis, selecting local private-network interface, opt-in rehosting at launch, encrypted reachability check, and explicit conflict handling.
+- Reminder: on-demand diagnostics/test notification, permission request from due/reminder editor, reschedule on resume.
+- Flow: Material ancestor for standalone route and drag adjusted for current zoom factor.
+- A voluntary honesty pledge displayed in Journey.
+- Long subject folder labels truncate rather than overflow; compact phone heading.
+- Tests for calendar multiple tasks and descriptions, standalone Flow, notes and Help.
+
+## Still requiring validation / limitations
+- No guarantee the inherited Flutter `_dependents.isEmpty` assertion is eliminated; it may require a full Android stack trace with reproduction steps.
+- Local network sync still rejects conflicting independent edits rather than merging records and cannot work across subnets without router configuration.
+- Android inexact alarms may arrive later than their scheduled time depending on battery policy. Notifications must be enabled in the app and system; Android manufacturer restrictions vary.
+- Notes use the existing synced note body; color choice is device-local. No automatic multi-device syncing of note colors yet.
+- Diagram editor is not at diagram.net feature parity (connector editing, grouping, shape libraries, undo/redo).
+- Real-device testing and release signing are still required.
